# Code this repo commits but the map is NOT meant to describe.
#
# `eval/fixtures/trapdoor/` is a synthetic codebase built to TRIP coyodex's own advisories —
# broken anchors, overclaimed edges, an oversized flat folder, a generated dir. Left in the
# analysed tree it would inflate the weight map, skew the component expectation E, and show up
# forever as an unreferenced directory in coyodex's self-map. It is not part of the product.
#
# ONE entry is the whole file, and it is deliberately the only one. A wildcard-free pattern covers
# everything beneath it, so the artifacts a build OVER the fixture writes back into it
# (`eval/fixtures/trapdoor/.coyodex/`, `.coyodex-eval/`) are already inside this line — and both of
# those names are built-in exclusions besides. Naming them again would add patterns that remove
# nothing, which `validate` now reports as patterns that decided nothing. If you add a line here,
# check the count it reports: a zero means the line is not doing what you think.
eval/fixtures/trapdoor/
